{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"28":{"eng-name":"Foods (Kitab Al-At'imah)","ara-name":"كتاب الأطعمة"}},"section_detail":{"28":{"hadithnumber_first":3736,"hadithnumber_last":3854,"arabicnumber_first":3736,"arabicnumber_last":3854}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":3801,"arabicnumber":3801,"text":"Rapporté par Jabir ibn Abdullah : J’ai interrogé le Messager d’Allah ﷺ au sujet de la hyène. Il a répondu : « C’est une bête de chasse, et si quelqu’un en état d’ihram la chasse, il doit offrir un mouton en compensation. »","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}],"reference":{"book":28,"hadith":66},"chapter":{"id":32,"ara-name":"باب فِي أَكْلِ الضَّبُعِ","eng-name":"Regarding eating hyena","isFirstHadith":true}}]}